    "Boat anglers caught Chinook salmon 25 to 100 feet down in 45 to 120 feet of water.",
    "Orange, blue and green spoons were reported to have worked well.",
    "Flasher-fly combinations caught a few salmon deeper in the water column.",
    "Pier anglers did well casting spoons for freshwater drum.",
    "A few steelhead were caught using shrimp under a bobber.",
    "Be sure to check your lines often.",
    "Salmon anglers targeting waters shallower than 80 feet found high numbers of small Chinook less than 18 inches."
